"The Here-to-There home ritual is sat in concentric rings, passing wood chips right to left."
"Each holder speaks home words with images while a master wizard chants and throws ingredients."
"It runs until sunrise; breath syncs, a trance deepens, and each will strengthens the others."
"'To strengthen one is to strengthen all': clasped hands let one hear another's thought of home."
"Longing, hope, imagining, or one treasured memory are enough to make a chip glow."
"It ends in a fireball; glowing chips become charms for harmony and fertility of land and body."
"Locals bury their chips around the pavilion; travelers take theirs home to bury."
